# A copy of a spell is not cast (CR 707.10), so a copy of Faerie Fencing never "controlled a Faerie as you cast this spell": the
# ruling on the Dragon spells' same condition, "the copy wasn't cast, so whether you controlled a Dragon won't matter". The copy
# does copy X (CR 707.10). Bot1 controls Faerie Mastermind as it casts Fencing with X = 0 at Bot2's Rot-Curse Rakshasa (5/5), then
# flashes in Lutri, the Spellchaser, whose enters trigger copies Fencing with the same target. The copy resolves first: -0/-0 and
# no bonus; then the original: -0/-0 and -3/-3. The Rakshasa is 2/2 (had the copy the bonus too, -6/-6 would kill it).

